# Custom Analog Audio Distortion Pedal & Enclosure

A custom analog audio distortion pedal featuring an NPN transistor gain stage, diode clipping network, and a custom 3D-modeled SolidWorks enclosure. This project showcases the full product lifecycle from circuit simulation and CAD tolerancing to physical assembly and signal analysis.

---

## 🛠️ Key Technical Highlights

* **CAD & Mechanical Design:** Modeled a custom enclosure in SolidWorks featuring extruded sliding channels for an acrylic viewing window and precision cutouts for ¼" audio jacks and control pots[cite: 1].
* **Manufacturing & Tolerancing:** Drafted fully dimensioned ANSI-standard mechanical drawings to manage geometric tolerances for 3D printing and internal PCB fitment[cite: 1].
* **Circuit Simulation:** Designed and simulated the NPN transistor gain stage and soft-clipping diode network in NI Multisim[cite: 1].
* **Hardware Validation:** Evaluated harmonic distortion across audio frequency ranges using a function generator and digital storage oscilloscope[cite: 1].

