## 📐 Mechanical Design & Enclosure (SolidWorks)

The enclosure was designed from the ground up in SolidWorks with Design for Manufacturing (DFM) and assembly constraints in mind[cite: 1]:

* **Acrylic Viewing Window:** Designed extruded sliding channels into the main housing body to allow a clear acrylic sheet to slide into place without requiring extra fasteners[cite: 1].
* **Interference & Clearance Fit:** Calculated spatial clearances and geometric tolerances for internal mounting cutouts, audio jacks, switches, and PCB dimensions[cite: 1].
* **Technical Drawings:** Created ANSI-standard fully dimensioned drawings to drive rapid 3D printing iterations[cite: 1].

